  <!-- SECTION 4: DATA HOSTED AT MAIZEGDB -->
  <section id="flints-data-hosted" aria-labelledby="flints-hosted-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="flints-hosted-title">Hosted data</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="flints-hosted-grid">
      <!-- 1: JBrowse 2 -->
      <article class="flints-hosted-card">
        <h3>Genome Browsers \(JBrowse 2\)</h3>
        <p>Interactive chromosome-scale browsers for DK105, EP1, F7, and PE0075 featuring gene models, RepeatMasker TE tracks, RNA-seq alignments, and synteny views.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/genomebrowser">Open Genome Browsers &#8599;</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 2: Gene Center -->
      <article class="flints-hosted-card">
        <h3>Gene Center &amp; Models</h3>
        <p>Over 40,000 high-confidence gene models per assembly indexed in the Gene Center with functional annotations, GO terms, and cross-references.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/gene_center/gene">Explore Gene Center &#8599;</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 3: BLAST -->
      <article class="flints-hosted-card">
        <h3>Sequence BLAST Tool</h3>
        <p>Align nucleotide, CDS, transcript, and translated protein queries directly against European flint genome assemblies and gene models.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="$(blast_url)">Run BLAST Search &#8599;</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 4: Bulk Downloads -->
      <article class="flints-hosted-card">
        <h3>Bulk Downloads &amp; Globus</h3>
        <p>Retrieve whole-genome FASTA, GFF3 annotations, canonical CDS/PEP sequences, and pre-indexed tracks via HTTP or Globus.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/download#downloads-flints">Browse Downloads &#8599;</a>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: SCALE & GENOMIC METRICS DASHBOARD -->
  <section id="flints-faqs" aria-labelledby="flints-faqs-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="flints-faqs-title">FAQs</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="flints-faq-list">
      <details class="flints-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>How do European flint gene models compare to the B73 RefGen_v5 reference?</h3></summary>
        <div class="flints-faq-body">
          <p>
            The European flint assemblies were annotated with the TUM-1.0 pipeline using comprehensive RNA-seq evidence and cross-species homology. While the core gene set shares ~85% 1:1 syntenic orthology with B73 RefGen_v5, each flint line carries 2,000–3,500 non-syntenic or duplicated genes, particularly enriched in abiotic stress response and cell wall biosynthesis pathways.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="flints-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Where can I download the complete FASTA and GFF3 annotation files?</h3></summary>
        <div class="flints-faq-body">
          <p>
            Complete genome sequences, soft-masked FASTA files, GFF3 gene annotations, CDS sequences, and protein translations are available on the <a href="/download#downloads-flints">MaizeGDB Downloads Page</a>, via direct HTTPS links in the table above, or through the NCBI GenBank repository.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="flints-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>How should I cite the European flint genome assemblies in publications?</h3></summary>
        <div class="flints-faq-body">
          <p>
            Please cite the landmark paper&#58; <strong>Haberer et al. \(2020\)</strong>, <em>European maize genomes highlight intraspecies variation in repeat and gene content</em>, Nature Genetics 52, 950–957 \(<a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-020-0671-9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi&#58;10.1038/s41588-020-0671-9</a>\), along with the specific assembly accession numbers and MaizeGDB database citation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="flints-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Can I run BLAST against individual European flint assemblies?</h3></summary>
        <div class="flints-faq-body">
          <p>
            Yes! MaizeGDB hosts dedicated BLAST databases for all four flint lines. Navigate to the <a href="$(blast_url)">BLAST Tool</a> and select the desired European flint assembly or predicted peptide database from the target sequence dropdown menu.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: CONNECTED RESOURCES -->
  <section id="flints-metrics" aria-labelledby="flints-metrics-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="flints-metrics-title">Metrics</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="mgdb-metric-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>De novo reference assemblies</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value">4</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">DK105, EP1, F7, and PE0075 representing major Central European flint founder lineages.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>Genome assembly size</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">~2.3 Gb</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">High-continuity chromosome-scale scaffolds capturing ~95% of estimated flint genome content.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>Retrotransposon dynamics</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value">1.6&times;</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">1.6-fold faster LTR retrotransposon turnover rate compared to US dent lines \(B73\).</p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>Gene models per assembly</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">40,000+</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">High-confidence TUM-1.0 structural and functional gene annotations per inbred line.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: FAQS & GUIDELINES -->
  <section id="flints-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="flints-related-title">
